message.content:
The bug is this line:

```go
go func() {
    defer wg.Done()
    fmt.Println(i)
}()
```

The anonymous function captures the loop variable `i` by reference. In Go 1.21, the loop variable `i` is reused across all iterations, so by the time these goroutines actually run, the loop has already finished and `i` is `5`. That’s why you see `5 5 5 5 5`.

Fix it by passing the current loop value into the goroutine as an argument:

<solution language="go" verdict="fix">
package main

import (
    "fmt"
    "sync"
)

func main() {
    var wg sync.WaitGroup
    for i := 0; i < 5; i++ {
        wg.Add(1)
        go func(n int) {
            defer wg.Done()
            fmt.Println(n)
        }(i)
    }
    wg.Wait()
}
</solution>

