message.content:
The bug is that `positive` and `negative` are initialized from the same backing array:

```go
positive := nums[:0]
negative := nums[:0]
```

Because both slices share the same underlying storage as `nums`, appending to one slice can overwrite data used by the other slice. That is why the returned slices get corrupted.

<solution language="go" verdict="fix">
func filterPositiveAndNegative(nums []int) ([]int, []int) {
    positive := make([]int, 0, len(nums))
    negative := make([]int, 0, len(nums))

    for _, n := range nums {
        if n > 0 {
            positive = append(positive, n)
        } else if n < 0 {
            negative = append(negative, n)
        }
    }
    return positive, negative
}
</solution>

